{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1158213-real-life-masquerade-breaches","id":1158213,"title":"\"Real Life\" Masquerade Breaches","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-13T10:40:23-08:00","id":1158213,"title":"\"Real Life\" Masquerade Breaches","content":"Recently I've read about an historic incident called the<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Highgate_Vampire\" target=\"_blank\"> Highgate Vampire</a>, an instance which eventually lead into a mass &quot;vampire hunting&quot; during the 1970, and that made me think- in the world of the CofD, just how angry/scared London's vampires would be from the event, whether if it was a vampire who let down their guard- or a mortal who knew too much made an unlucky guess. <br /> <br /> Because of that, I've decided to make a thread dedicated for any historic real life instances which could be, in Requiem, be presented as instances where the Masquerade broke down, and why it is so important for the Kindred to deal with the breaches before it becomes too late. You know, something that elders tell to neonates about why they should take the whole thing seriously, and how stupid it would be to not uphold the Masquerade- I mean, do you want a mass vampire hunting? That's how you get a mass vampire hunting.<br /> <br /> So- what potential breaches do you have in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://ch